      "message": "nit (I recently learned about this pattern matching):\n```\nlet chunks \u003d cells.chunks_exact(2);\n\nwhile let Some([phandle, sid]) \u003d chunks.next() {\n    let phandle \u003d Phandle::try_from(phandle).or(...)?;\n    let iommu \u003d phys_iommus.get(\u0026phandle).ok_or(...)?;\n    \n    iommus.push((*iommu, Sid::from(sid)));\n}\n\nif !chunks.remainder().is_empty() {\n    return Err(...);\n}\n```\nNote that you could also make use of `Phandle as From\u003cu32\u003e`:\n```\nlet iommu \u003d Phandle::from(phandle).and_then(|p| phys_iommus.get(\u0026p)).ok_or(...)?;\n```\n\n(same in `AssignedDeviceInfo::parse_iommus()`)",
